Seed: Split and Values(step) end when n × step alone overflows, though start + n × step still fits, on Int64Range, DecimalRange, Float64Range and Float32Range
Oracles: RangeSplitOracleTests
Fails: the half-domain row of each of the four types: the walk stops one or two steps early and the last piece is wider than the step
History: shipped in the 10.0.0 previews, found by the pre-tag analysis, fixed in 10.0.0 (#219)

diff --git a/src/CodoMetis.ValueRanges/DecimalRange.cs b/src/CodoMetis.ValueRanges/DecimalRange.cs
index 2142507..defcf7b 100644
--- a/src/CodoMetis.ValueRanges/DecimalRange.cs
+++ b/src/CodoMetis.ValueRanges/DecimalRange.cs
@@ -202,7 +202,7 @@ public abstract partial record DecimalRange : IRange<decimal>, IRangeFactory<Dec
     public IEnumerable<DecimalRange> Split(decimal step)
     {
         ArgumentOutOfRangeException.ThrowIfNegativeOrZero(step);
-        return RangeSplitting.Split<DecimalRange, decimal>(this, RangeSplitting.Steps<decimal>(this, (start, n) => checked(start + n * step), previous => checked(previous + step)));
+        return RangeSplitting.Split<DecimalRange, decimal>(this, RangeSplitting.Steps<decimal>(this, (start, n) => checked(start + n * step)));
     }
 
